      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Benztropine:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " usual 1 to 2 mg/day PO (range 0.5 to 6 mg); idiopathic parkinsonism may start at 0.5 to 1 mg at bedtime."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Benztropine may cause anhidrosis:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " use caution in hot weather, especially with other atropine-like drugs or manual labor in heat. With phenothiazines, haloperidol or other anticholinergic or antidopaminergic drugs, report GI complaints, fever or heat intolerance promptly (paralytic ileus, hyperthermia and heat stroke have sometimes been fatal)."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Anticholinergic intoxication:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " physostigmine 1 to 2 mg SC or IV reportedly reverses symptoms; otherwise treatment is symptomatic and supportive."
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
